  "prompt": "Yara, from retail operations, found store orders booked after midnight in the daily store report, when every store is closed. These tables may hold errors. The report reads every order_ts as UTC and turns it into Amsterdam time. In fact a store order's order_ts holds the store's local time (stores.timezone), and a web order's holds UTC. Which stores does the report hit, and how hard? Return one row for each store with at least one order, the webshop included, with four columns in this order: store_id; store_code; n_orders, all of the store's orders; and n_wrong_day, its orders that the report puts on another day than the Amsterdam day they were really placed on. Sort by store_id from low to high.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "store_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "store_code",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "n_orders",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
